§ `ss 4, 6, 7, 8 -- how it becomes spent`

#ASSERT `How can my conviction become spent` `a fine of $500 on 20 November 2021` (Date 20 11 2026) EQUALS `not yet: the prescribed period has not expired`
#ASSERT `How can my conviction become spent` `a fine of $500 on 20 November 2021` (Date 20 11 2031) EQUALS `apply to the Commissioner of Police, who must issue a certificate (s 7)`
#ASSERT `How can my conviction become spent` `18 months' imprisonment on 1 March 2010` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS `apply to a District Court judge, who decides at discretion (s 6)`
#ASSERT `How can my conviction become spent` `18 months in 2010, refused on 1 June 2025` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS `not yet: a judge refused an order within the last 2 years`
#ASSERT `How can my conviction become spent` `18 months in 2010, refused on 1 June 2025` (Date 1 7 2027) EQUALS `apply to a District Court judge, who decides at discretion (s 6)`
#ASSERT `How can my conviction become spent` `life imprisonment in 2000` (Date 4 3 2047) EQUALS `never under s 6 or 7: the sentence included life imprisonment`
#ASSERT `How can my conviction become spent` `a Queensland conviction spent under Queensland law` (Date 20 11 2026) EQUALS `only under its own jurisdiction's law, which Schedule 2 recognises`
#ASSERT `How can my conviction become spent` `a youth conviction that has stopped counting` (Date 4 3 2047) EQUALS `not under Part 2: a youth conviction stops counting under Young Offenders Act 1994 s 189`

-- s 7(1): a lesser conviction is spent only when the certificate issues, however long ago it was.
