-- k036 and k082 (the job form at 40, 4 March 2047): nothing for the Act to act on, in any role.
#ASSERT `Must I disclose it` `Jake's shop theft, sent to a juvenile justice team` `none of the Schedule 3 roles` `a question put to me, or to someone else about me` EQUALS `nothing for this Act to act on: no conviction and no charge in court`
#ASSERT `Must I disclose it` `Jake's shop theft, sent to a juvenile justice team` `a licence or permit under the Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996` `a question put to me, or to someone else about me` EQUALS `nothing for this Act to act on: no conviction and no charge in court`
#ASSERT `Must I disclose it` `a youth theft conviction that has stopped counting` `none of the Schedule 3 roles` `a question put to me, or to someone else about me` EQUALS `no: the question is taken not to relate to it (s 27(1))`
#ASSERT `Must I disclose it` `a spent theft conviction` `none of the Schedule 3 roles` `a question put to me, or to someone else about me` EQUALS `no: the question is taken not to relate to it (s 27(1))`
#ASSERT `Must I disclose it` `a spent theft conviction` `a licence or permit under the Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996` `a question put to me, or to someone else about me` EQUALS `yes: Schedule 3 excepts my role from this protection`
#ASSERT `Must I disclose it` `a spent theft conviction` `none of the Schedule 3 roles` `a written law of Western Australia that requires disclosure` EQUALS `no: the written law does not require it (s 25(2))`
#ASSERT `Must I disclose it` `a spent theft conviction` `a working with children check (Working with Children (Screening) Act 2004 s 34)` `a written law of Western Australia that requires disclosure` EQUALS `no: the written law does not require it (s 25(2))`
#ASSERT `Must I disclose it` `a spent theft conviction` `a working with children check (Working with Children (Screening) Act 2004 s 34)` `a question put to me, or to someone else about me` EQUALS `yes: Schedule 3 excepts my role from this protection`
#ASSERT `Must I disclose it` `a spent theft conviction` `none of the Schedule 3 roles` `a court or tribunal that applies the laws of evidence` EQUALS `yes: the protection does not apply before a court or tribunal that applies the laws of evidence (s 14)`
#ASSERT `Must I disclose it` `a spent theft conviction` `none of the Schedule 3 roles` `my own application to a District Court judge under s 6` EQUALS `yes: the application must set out all previous convictions (Schedule 1 cl 1; s 14)`
#ASSERT `Must I disclose it` `an unspent theft conviction` `none of the Schedule 3 roles` `a question put to me, or to someone else about me` EQUALS `this Act does not excuse it: the conviction is not spent`
#ASSERT `Must I disclose it` `a charge withdrawn in court` `none of the Schedule 3 roles` `an agreement, an arrangement, or a rule of common law or equity` EQUALS `no: the agreement or rule does not require it (s 27(2))`
#ASSERT `Must I disclose it` `a conviction deemed not a conviction under an old Act` `none of the Schedule 3 roles` `a question put to me, or to someone else about me` EQUALS `no: the question is taken not to relate to it (s 27(1))`
#ASSERT `Must I disclose it` `a spent theft conviction` `employment in a care centre, preschool centre or child care service` `a question put to me, or to someone else about me` EQUALS `no: the question is taken not to relate to it (s 27(1))`
#ASSERT `Must I disclose it` `a spent sexual offence conviction` `employment in a care centre, preschool centre or child care service` `a question put to me, or to someone else about me` EQUALS `yes: Schedule 3 excepts my role from this protection`
#ASSERT `Must I disclose it` `a spent assault conviction, the victim a child` `employment in a care centre, preschool centre or child care service` `a question put to me, or to someone else about me` EQUALS `yes: Schedule 3 excepts my role from this protection`

